  "body": "**Stacked on #676** (#670, plasma profile), which is stacked on #674 (#669, plasma kind). Review only this PR's own commit, `2645a023`.\n\nA **PathPilot plasma post for the Tormach 1300PL** (#671). Every word below was checked against UM10720 v1223A ([UM]) or Tormach's PathPilot Post Processor Guidelines, Plasma column ([PG]).\n\n| Word | Meaning | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `G20`/`G21` | units | [PG] |\n| `G90 G91.1 G94 G17 G40 G49 G80` | modal reset, once | [PG]; [UM] §6.2.2 |\n| `G64 P0.005 Q0.005` | path blending (P in inches even under G21) | [UM] §6.2.1 p.50; [PG] |\n| `G54` | work offset | [UM] §6.2.1 |\n| `G43 H1` | torch length offset | [PG] (\"always H1\"); [UM] §6.2.2 |\n| `G30` | go to the G30 height | [UM] §6.2.1-6.2.2 |\n| `G0 X Y` | rapid to the pierce point, never Z | [UM] §6.2.1 |\n| `M200` | AutoFS (feed, THC volts, pierce height and delay, amps) | [UM] §6.3 p.51, §7.2 p.54 |\n| `M207`/`M208`/`M209 P` | pierce height / cut height / pierce delay, only when the op states them | [UM] §6.3.1 p.52, §7.2 |\n| `G15` | ohmic probe; WCS Z = 0 | [UM] §7.1 p.54 |\n| `G16` | rise to pierce height, fire, delay, go to cut height, THC on | [UM] §7.1; [PG] |\n| `G1/G2/G3 X Y [I J] [F]` | the cut, XY only | [PG] |\n| `G41.1`/`G42.1 D<kerf>` … `G40` | control compensation, each on its own line before a straight lead | [PG] |\n| `M205` | torch off, Z to the G30 height | [UM] §7.2 |\n| `M30` | end | [PG] |\n\n- **Never written:** S, M3-M9, M6, G95-G99, canned cycles.\n- **M6 conflict:** [PG] says M6 is unsupported on plasma, but [UM]'s test program writes `T1 M6`. This follows the issue and [PG]; the conflict is recorded.\n\n## What changed\n- **Script:** `assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps`, registered as \"Tormach PathPilot Plasma\", the only `PLASMA_POSTS` entry. Milling posts decline a plasma stream, because they lack the torch hooks.\n- **Stream:** #676's records are carried into the post stream: `PLASMA …`, `TORCH ON C<id> …` and `TORCH OFF C<id>` (the `.cl` v5 records without `; `).\n  - The parser reads both spellings; malformed records are refused by line number.\n  - New properties: `PlasmaKerf`, `PlasmaCompensation`, `PierceHeight`, `CutHeight`, `PierceDelay` (absent = AutoFS), `PlasmaFeed`, `PlasmaReversed`, `Contour`, `ContourRole`, `ParentContour`, `SmallHole`.\n  - New hooks: `onPlasma`, `onTorchOn`, `onTorchOff`.\n  - `machine.kind` is now a script property.\n- **Engine torch law** (`cnc_torch.rs`), refused by name:\n  - a TORCH with no header, a second header;\n  - ON while lit, a wrong or extra OFF, a rapid while lit;\n  - a section or stream left lit;\n  - a script without both torch hooks.\n- **Post refusals:**\n  - a non-plasma op, a Plasma Profile path with no plasma record;\n  - rpm, coolant (other than off), a rotary or tilted move;\n  - Z on a lit move, a canned cycle, a dark feed;\n  - comp under a computer offset, wear comp;\n  - a machine that isn't `kind: plasma`.\n- **AutoFS:** under AUTOFEED, no F is written. A small hole then runs at the AutoFS feed, with an operator comment; refusing it would block every default plate with a hole.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/671-plasma-post.md` (the sources and ten choices). CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md and assets/posts/AGENTS.md are updated.\n\n## Golden (`tormach-plasma/plasma_plate_with_holes.nc`, inch; excerpt)\n```\nG20\nG90 G91.1 G94 G17 G40 G49 G80\nG64 P0.005 Q0.005\n(T1 PLASMA TORCH - KERF 0.0591)\nG54\nG43 H1\nG30\n(C0 INNER IN C4 - SMALL HOLE 65% FEED)\nG0 X3.3465 Y0.7874\nM200\nM207 P0.1496\nM209 P0.5\nG15\nG16\nG1 X3.3465 Y0.9547 F63.98\n...\nM205\nG30\n```\nSiblings: `_mm.nc` and `_control.nc` (`G41.1 D0.0591` … `G40`). The CLI post is byte-identical to the inch golden.\n\n## How tested\n- **`plasma_post` (5):**\n  - the inch and mm goldens, with structural checks: no Z/S/T/M3-M9/M6, per-contour order, G30 after every M205, ending `G30 M30`;\n  - the in-app dump equals the `.cl` golden;\n  - the control-comp golden;\n  - a stream round-trip, plus malformed-record refusals;\n  - an in-app 1300PL document posts through the gate.\n- **`plasma_post_refusals` (5):** every refusal, the engine torch law, every milling builtin declining the stream, and the registry.\n- **Pins updated:** plasma_machine, machine_library, plasma_profile, golden_cl and conformance.\n- **Gate:**\n  - those suites plus posting, camcraft-post and camcraft-cl;\n  - also tormach_post, control_comp, coolant, after_op, program_comments, fanuc_post, lathe_post, per_op_files and probe_guard;\n  - clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (why this is a draft): a PathPilot Hub 1300PL simulator run\nIt should check:\n1. G20 and G21 both load and run, and `G64 P0.005 Q0.005` reads as inches under G21.\n2. `G43 H1` without `T1 M6` is accepted.\n3. Whether a bare `G30` after `M205` also travels XY (a time cost only).\n4. `M207`/`M209` after `M200` override AutoFS.\n5. G1 moves with no F take the AutoFS feed.\n6. `G41.1 D…` on its own line, a straight lead, then `G40`, with the offset on the right side.\n7. G2/G3 under G91.1.\n8. Probe and pierce at each G0 point, THC on, M205, and the part matches.\n\nChangelog: A PathPilot plasma post for the Tormach 1300PL: M200 AutoFS, G15 probe, G16 pierce, M205 torch off, G30; G41.1/G42.1 D<kerf> under control compensation; non-plasma work refused by name (#671)\n\nFixes #671\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
